-- title:
--   Finite places of ℚ are generated by rational primes
-- statement:
--   Let $v$ be a point of the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, the ring of integers of the number field $\mathbb{Q}$, i.e. $v$ is a nonzero prime ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ of height one (in Mathlib's formulation, an element of `IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 ℚ)`, whose underlying ideal is written `v.asIdeal`). The assertion is that there exists a natural number $p$ which is prime in the sense of `Nat.Prime` such that the ideal $v.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ coincides with the principal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the image of $p$ under the canonical map $\mathbb{N} \to \mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, that is, $v.\mathrm{asIdeal} = (p)$. No further hypotheses are imposed; the base field is fixed to be $\mathbb{Q}$, so the result is the concrete classification of the finite places of $\mathbb{Q}$ by rational primes rather than any statement about general number fields.
--
--   This is the identification of the nonzero primes of $\mathbb{Z} = \mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ with the rational primes, packaged in the height-one-spectrum language in which adelic and local data over $\mathbb{Q}$ are phrased. It supplies the case-split on a rational prime $p$ needed whenever an argument about an arbitrary finite place of $\mathbb{Q}$ must be reduced to the completion $\mathbb{Q}_p$; the estimates on Fourier coefficients of automorphic forms and the Deligne–Serre weight-one results in this development invoke it in exactly this way.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDedekindDomain_HeightOneSpectrum_exists_prime_and_asIdeal_eq_span_ringOfIntegers_rat.lean

